 "notes": [
  "FY2009 figures come only from the comparative column of the 2010 registration document (2011-04-18_hermes_2010_rapportannuel_en.txt); no 2009 document was processed.",
  "FY2006-2008: revenue, ROI, operating income, net income, operating cash flows, 'Investments (excluding financial investments)' (recorded as cf.capex with negative sign), shareholders' equity excl. NCI, net cash, restated net cash and headcount from 'KEY CONSOLIDATED DATA' (2011-04-18_hermes_2010_rapportannuel_en.txt, Key figures p.21). 2006 revenue printed as '1 514.9'. Equity 2007/2008 footnoted 'after application of IAS 38 on samples and advertising/promotional expenditure'.",
  "FY2007/2006 operating income (423.7/415.2) exceeds ROI (414.5/401.1): non-recurring income of 9.2 / 14.1 implied (not itemised in 2011-04-18_hermes_2010_rapportannuel_en.txt).",
  "FY2008 eps_basic 2.76, wavg shares 105,074,019 and shares outstanding 105,550,012 from 'KEY STOCK MARKET DATA' (2011-04-18_hermes_2010_rapportannuel_en.txt, p.22); FY2008 operating investments 155.4 from 'Breakdown of investments' (2011-04-18_hermes_2010_rapportannuel_en.txt, p.97). Consolidated EPS for 2006/2007 not printed in 2011-04-18_hermes_2010_rapportannuel_en.txt (only parent-company EPS) -> omitted.",
  "DPS 2006 0.95 (after 3-for-1 split of 10 June 2006), 2007 1.00, 2008 1.03, 2009 1.05 from the parent-company five-year summary (2011-04-18_hermes_2010_rapportannuel_en.txt, p.207) and AGM resolution table; shares outstanding 2007 106,089,214 and 2006 106,874,814 from the same five-year summary.",
  "Sector/region revenue for 2006-2008: 2011-04-18_hermes_2010_rapportannuel_en.txt contains no multi-year numeric table by métier or region (only 2010 vs 2009 tables and pie-chart %s) -> not recorded.",
  "Sector revenue 2009, 2010 (2011-04-18_hermes_2010_rapportannuel_en.txt) and 2011 (2012-04-11_hermes_2011_rapportannuel_en.txt) are only printed in whole EUR millions (management report 'Activity by sector'); 2012 and 2013 use the decimal figures of Note 3.2 'Revenue by métier'. 2013-04-15_hermes_2012_rapportannuel_en.txt Note 3.2 gives 2011 comparatives with decimals: leather 1,348.0, rtw 575.7, silk 346.9, other Hermès 108.6, perfumes 159.4, watches 138.7, tableware 50.8, other products 113.1, total 2,841.2.",
  "2010/2011 sector tables also show subtotals 'Hermès Distribution Network' (2010: 2,021; 2009: 1,601; 2011: 2,379) and 'Specialised distribution networks' (2010: 294; 2009: 242; 2011: 349) - not mapped. 2010 cc growth Hermès network 19.0%, specialised 17.8%.",
  "Geo cc growth figures are from the management-report 'Activity by region' tables ('Other' = rest of world incl. Middle East, airlines). Geographic ROI = 'Operating income' by area in Note 3 (no non-recurring items in 2009-2013, so op income = ROI); roi_unalloc = 'Holding'.",
  "Cash flow statements 2009-2013 use the old layout: no single 'Operating investments' line (purchase of intangible assets and of PP&E are separate lines in cf_other), so cf.capex is null; apm.operating_investments is taken from the 'Breakdown of investments' table. 'Investments in associates' kept in cf_other. Three FX/scope lines: 'Effect of foreign currency exchange' mapped to cf.fx; 'Effect of changes in the scope of consolidation' and 'Effect of foreign currency exchange on intragroup transactions' in cf_other (all three needed to reconcile d_cash).",
  "Depreciation & amortisation and impairment losses are separate CF lines in 2009-2013: memo.da_cf / cf.da = D&A line only; impairment CF line is in cf_other. memo.da_fixed = D&A in Note 6 'Other income and expense' (excludes D&A in cost of sales); memo.impairment = impairment line of Note 6.",
  "BS: 'Investment property' (not in schema) is in bs_other; reval_adj = 'Derivatives/Financial instruments included in equity'; equity_parent taken from the statement of changes in equity (not a line on the balance sheet). 'Fair value of financial instruments'/'Derivative financial instruments' mapped to derivatives_a/derivatives_l.",
  "2011: net financial income +12.4 includes a EUR 29.5m gross capital gain on the sale of the 45% stake in Jean Paul Gaultier (Gaulme group); recorded in financial result, not taxable (2012-04-11_hermes_2011_rapportannuel_en.txt, Note 2 and p.96). CF 'Capital gains/(losses) on disposals' -28.7.",
  "2011 dividend: ordinary EUR 2.00 (interim 1.50 paid 1 March 2012) plus EXCEPTIONAL dividend EUR 5.00 per share in respect of FY2011, paid 5 June 2012 (2012-04-11_hermes_2011_rapportannuel_en.txt, AGM resolutions p.223); total 7.00. Cash dividends paid in 2012 = 742.3 incl. ~502.5 exceptional (2013-04-15_hermes_2012_rapportannuel_en.txt, p.99).",
  "2011 share buyback: 1,292,215 shares for EUR 286.0m (2012-04-11_hermes_2011_rapportannuel_en.txt, Note 20); treasury shares rose to 1,521,540.",
  "2012: goodwill impairment EUR 25.0m (HCP tannery CGU, Note 10) included in Other income and expense; Note 6 line printed as 'Depreciation and amortisation of property, plants and equipment (3.0)' is the impairment-loss line (relabelled 'Reversible impairment losses' in 2014-04-09_hermes_2013_rapportannuel_en.txt) -> memo.impairment 3.0.",
  "2013: goodwill impairment EUR 17.0m (Note 10) within 'Other expense (including depreciation of goodwill)' in Other income and expenses. Tax includes EUR 7.9m 3% tax on dividend distributions (memo.excep_tax 7.9, expense). French rate includes exceptional surcharge of 5% (2011-2012) / 10.7% (2013); amounts not disclosed (2014-04-09_hermes_2013_rapportannuel_en.txt, Note 8.2).",
  "Interim dividends: 2010 EUR 1.00 (paid 10 Feb 2011, first ever), 2011 1.50, 2012 1.50 (paid 1 Mar 2013), 2013 1.50 (paid 28 Feb 2014). DPS 2013 2.70 proposed (2014-04-09_hermes_2013_rapportannuel_en.txt).",
  "No restatements of prior-year comparatives were found in the 2011-2013 documents (comparatives agree with originally reported figures).",
  "Dashes in statements recorded as 0.0 (e.g., 'Other non-recurring income and expense' = 0.0 every year).",
  "Rounding: 2013 gross profit printed 2,584.4 vs 3,754.8-1,170.3=2,584.5; 2012 total equity on BS 2,358.3 vs 2,358.2 in statement of changes; 2013 FX reserve BS -33.4 vs -33.5 in statement of changes. Printed values kept."
